      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hoffman_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hoffman was originally part of McIntosh County until it was annexed to Okmulgee County in 1918.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hoffman_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early residents of Hoffman were primarily farmers who grew cotton, corn, and pecans while raising livestock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hoffman_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office was established in Hoffman by December 18, 1905, shortly after the town was settled.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoffman%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The name Hoffman may come from Roy V. Hoffman, an attorney, or a vice president of the Missouri, Oklahoma and Gulf Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
